      'The inlet runs far inland and was once fed by a seasonal stream, which meant that — unlike most of Ibiza — there was water here. Terraces and old fincas still sit on the slopes above, and further inland lies Sant Carles, the village this area long belonged to. North of it were the lead mines of S’Argentera, worked into the twentieth century for silver-bearing ore — one of the very few real industries Ibiza ever had besides salt. The resort at the head of the bay is a much later addition.',
