      'Formentera is the southernmost of the Balearic Islands, just below Ibiza. It has no airport: the only way in is by boat. The island is low and narrow, with a flat middle, a sand spit in the north and a higher plateau in the east. Its main town is Sant Francesc Xavier, inland.',
